///! Prelude
///!
///! The prelude is imported automatically into every Cryo source file. It
///! carries the short list of names that are universally useful — the things
///! that would add friction if you had to import them every time.
///!
///! Keeping the prelude small is a deliberate choice. Every name here competes
///! for user attention: the more that lives in the prelude, the harder it is
///! for a reader to tell whether a symbol is a language primitive, a stdlib
///! staple, or something the user defined. When in doubt, put it in an
///! explicit module.

namespace std::prelude;

public module core::panic;
public module core::option;
public module core::result;

// Phase 1 does NOT put Array, String, or Box in the prelude — those types
// don't exist in this phase yet. They come back in Phase 4/5.
